the identity is stable across two compiles of the same program: true
a code-borne knob (default_prec) changes the digest: true
and therefore the cache key: true
a materialized constant compiles identically in both constant-fill regimes (gh-633): true
a keyed codegen knob (large_models) leaves the digest alone: true
while the cache key separates the regimes: true
a cc codegen knob (cc_vector_bytes) leaves the digest alone: true
and separates the key exactly on the backend that reads it: true
search-shaping and execution-neutral knobs leave the identity untouched: true
placement-shaping knobs leave the identity untouched: true
raising the log level alone does not churn the key: true
nor does asking for routine logs the log level keeps switched off: true
while logs that actually reach the kernel separate the key: true
an aliasing flip separates the key without touching the digest: true
the OpenMP team size separates the key on the backend that runs OpenMP Grid loops: true
a numerics knob (tf32_matmuls) leaves the digest alone: true
while the cache key separates the policies: true
